## Project

SENTINEL-X is a research demonstrator for air-gapped reconnaissance on one
Jetson Orin NX 16GB. A person remains in the decision. It is not a weapon.
The MCXN947 is not part of this project. The board reports `GPU 0: Orin`.

Target event: defence / security expo, 24 September 2026, Essen.

## Pipeline

Run `python run.py` from the repo root.

1. Three YOLO detectors place boxes on `combined_drone.mp4`.
2. EfficientNet-B0 names each crop. Short side under 32 pixels is skipped.
3. Local Qwen (`qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_K_M`) answers from that text tally, only up to the frame on screen.

Package layout (`sentinel/`):
- `labels.py` - CNN class list, YOLO-to-CNN name map, weight/video path constants
- `detection.py` - YOLO loading, EfficientNet crop classifier, box dedup (merged from old jetson_test.py and join_and_detect_video.py)
- `chat.py` - Qwen streaming chat, greeting, object-query helpers
- `gpu.py` - GPU percent and free-memory reader (Orin + nvidia-smi)
- `window.py` - Tkinter demo window (renamed from Data/video/sentinel_demo.py)

Entry point: `run.py`. Tests: `tests/test_labels.py`, `tests/test_detection.py`, `tests/test_window.py` (49 tests, all pass).

Chat is 40 percent of the row, video 60 percent. Detection uses `cuda:0` and refuses CPU. A `.engine` beside a `.pt` is loaded when it exists. Overlapping boxes count once, keeping the higher EfficientNet score. A YOLO box EfficientNet did not name is not counted.

